# Expo Go + physical iPhone + local Supabase (canonical-only scan flow):
# 1) Run local stack and verify functions:
#      bash product/scripts/mobile-functions-smoke-check.sh
# 2) Start HTTPS tunnel:
#      bash product/scripts/start-supabase-https-tunnel.sh
#    then copy: https://<random>.trycloudflare.com
# 3) Put tunnel URL below as EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL.
#
# Local Supabase ports:
#   - API + Edge Functions: http://127.0.0.1:54321
#   - Studio (admin UI only): http://127.0.0.1:54323
#
# Get local anon key:
#   pnpm exec supabase status

# For Expo Go use HTTPS URL (tunnel or hosted project), not localhost.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://<random>.trycloudflare.com
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<local-anon-key>

# If you use `pnpm -C product/apps/consumer-mobile run start:expogo:tunnel`,
# Expo serves Metro through its own tunnel, so this LAN URL is not required.
# Keep it only for explicit LAN/dev-client workflows.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://192.168.1.106:8081

# Base URL of Next.js roaster UI (product/apps/web); used by cross-links and native app-link/universal-link
# host derivation for `https://<host>/q/{hash}`. For beta builds set the canonical HTTPS beta host.
# For hotspot / non-LAN usage this should be a reachable public HTTPS host, or can stay unset locally.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ROASTER_WEB_URL=https://<reachable-host>
